&lt;p&gt;At Sage Bionetworks, we believe in the power of open science and interdisciplinary collaboration to create a new vision of human health. We strive for actionable biomedical insights through the responsible sharing and reuse of data, all guided by our deep scientific expertise and diligent governance controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a dynamic, adaptable team, and at Sage, we highly value individuals who can flexibly navigate various roles and functions. Diversity in experiences, backgrounds, and identities is essential for our rich culture of learning and collaboration. Our partnerships, both within Sage and with external communities, are founded on principles of trust, transparency, and a commitment to growth. Together, we are leaving a lasting imprint on the fields of science and medicine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will be a member of the Alzheimer’s Disease Translational Research Team working on a variety of National Institutes on Aging-supported programs focused on Alzheimer’s Disease and other neurodegenerative diseases. You will apply your skill as an Alzheimer’s Disease Translational Research Intern by engaging in multi-omic research using data (transcriptomic, proteomic, epigenomic, metabolomic) from the AD Knowledge Portal and other public resources. The ideal candidate will have strong computational biology/ bioinformatics skills as applied to multi-omic data, and will have enthusiasm for engaging with scientists and researchers across many disciplines.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An example project might include applying pre-processing and normalization protocols for epigenetic, proteomic, and/or transcriptomic data, and running differential methylation/ expression analyses. Harmonization and meta-analysis across different cohorts, and comparisons across brain regions, will also be considered. These and other -omics data may also be evaluated for molecular profile changes across stages of Alzheimer&#39;s disease neuropathology (progression). This work may lead to a publication or co-authorship, posting processed data, summary files, and/or code on the AD Knowledge Portal so that interested investigators may build on the work (Sage’s motto: “Better Science Together”), and/or presenting your work to internal and external (academic) colleagues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Does a project like this sound exciting to you? Does this sound like a good fit for your skill set and research interests? Do you want to be an integral part of a team that includes computational biologists, research ethicists, software engineers, and data librarians? If so, you could be our next Intern!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scientific Research: Develop innovative research initiatives using exploratory and hypothesis-driven data analysis on complex, high-dimensional datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analysis and Modeling: Utilize advanced statistics, machine learning methods, and study design expertise to pose research questions and analyze and interpret data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Methods Development: Create and document new methods, pipelines, and tools for data analysis, and adhere to standards of reproducible research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dissemination: Communicate research findings through publication of peer-reviewed research papers, maintain detailed records, present to funders and collaborators, and participate in research conferences and workshops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;When is the position available and hourly rate:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-6 month position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full time or part time is ok&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remote or in-person is ok&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start date can be as soon as January 2027; Summer 2027 is also acceptable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position is an intern level position with an hourly wage of $35 - 40&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’d love to hear from you if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are passionate about open science and collaboration, working with complex data, and supporting scientific research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are pursuing or recently received a M.S. or Ph.D in Neuroscience, Computational Biology, Bioinformatics, Biostatistics, Epidemiology, or related discipline; or commensurate experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 1 year of research experience in a relevant field.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are experienced and well-versed in data extraction, data cleaning, complex statistical analysis, and machine learning techniques using tools like R or Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognize the importance of applying critical thinking and thoughtful practices in your role, striving to ensure inclusivity, accessibility, and relevance for everyone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt; &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;submit a 100% original cover letter and CV. We value your authentic voice and personal writing style. This role requires critical thinking and clear communication, and your application is the first demonstration of those skills.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Functions and Physical Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The following cognitive and physical activities outline the essential functions required for successful job performance. Reasonable accommodations may be provided to enable individuals with disabilities to fulfill these functions.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Physical Demands&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Extended periods of sitting at a desk and using a computer.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Repeated wrist, hand, and finger movements.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Requires clear vision for tasks like data analysis, transcribing, computer use, and reading.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Occasionally lifting or moving objects weighing up to 10 pounds.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Cognitive Demands&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Able to work effectively under deadlines.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Strong problem-solving and analytical skills.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Attention to detail and accuracy.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Flexibility to adapt to changing environments, priorities and multitask.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Additional Requirements&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Travel is required a minimum of two times per year for on-site events in Seattle, WA.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Effective verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Works well in a team and maintains professionalism.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Follows company policies, procedures, and relevant laws and regulations.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Note: This list is not exhaustive and may be subject to modification as job duties evolve.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sage Bionetworks is a nonprofit biomedical research organization that was founded in Seattle in 2009. We focus on advancing human health through open science practices and radical collaboration, with a view to breaking down existing silos in science and technology. Through our work, we guide responsible data sharing and reuse, benchmark scientific methods and results, and empower participants to be active partners in research. We are a bold team of scientists, engineers, product developers, governance specialists and business experts, working to bring data and communities together in unique ways that accelerate medical progress. As a growing organization, Sage is supported through a dynamic portfolio of competitive research grants, commercial partnerships, and philanthropic contributions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Sage Bionetworks, we implement equitable workplace strategies to guarantee fair compensation. Actual compensation is determined based on current market data, experience, and internal pay parity. This position is an intern level position with an hourly wage of $35 - 40.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;All interns are eligible for a number of benefits, including but not limited to:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Holidays&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Sick Time&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Personal Days&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to org-wide meetings, workshops, training, etc.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentorship program&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transportation Benefits, if applicable&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a distributed workforce and support remote/on-site/hybrid work arrangements within the United States. All interviews will be conducted virtually unless otherwise communicated.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Sage Bionetworks, we uphold equal employment opportunities for all employees and applicants without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability, marital status, or veteran status. We strictly prohibit discrimination and harassment based on these protected categories, in compliance with federal and state equal employment opportunity laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’d like to request a &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/laws/guidance/job-applicants-and-ada&quot;&gt;reasonable accommodation,&lt;/a&gt; please let HR know prior to your interview.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sage Bionetworks uses open science and collaboration to improve human health. We bring together scientific, technical, and operational expertise to advance biomedical research through responsible data sharing, strong governance, and innovative approaches to research and technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work is complex, interdisciplinary, and mission-driven. We value curiosity, diverse perspectives, experimentation, accountability, and radical collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sage Bionetworks is seeking an Associate Director, Computational Biology to lead and grow a multidisciplinary team focused on applied scientific research, biomedical data stewardship, and community engagement around Sage’s data assets, including widely used resources such as Synapse, the AD Knowledge Portal, and the Cancer Complexity Knowledge Portal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a scientific and people leadership role with an opportunity to shape how Sage curates, governs, shares, and activates its biomedical data. You will establish scientific direction, data management standards, and community-engagement practices in partnership with Sage’s governance and platform teams. Your work will help ensure Sage’s data are Findable, Accessible, Interoperable, and Reusable (FAIR), aligned with GA4GH data-sharing standards, and trusted and actively used by the research community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead a multidisciplinary team of biomedical data managers, biomedical data engineers, community engagement staff, and program managers. You’ll also serve as a strategic partner to organizational leadership, connect data stewardship and community initiatives to Sage’s broader mission, identify opportunities to expand adoption of Sage’s data assets, and contribute to platform development priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Externally, you will represent Sage with data generators, researchers, funders, consortium partners, and other stakeholders. You will communicate the scientific value of Sage’s managed data, data derivatives, and software platforms while identifying community needs and opportunities for growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role combines scientific leadership, people leadership, and hands-on technical work. You will develop your team, strengthen Sage’s data stewardship and community capabilities, and continue contributing directly through computational biology, statistical, and bioinformatic work. The role is intentionally focused on applied, data- and community-oriented science rather than maintaining an independent, hypothesis-driven research program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The current scope includes substantial work with spatial and imaging data. You should have the practical technical understanding needed to design effective approaches for complex datasets, including large-scale, multi-omic data, and to evaluate emerging assays, data modalities, and computational methods.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll know you&#39;re succeeding when:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sage’s biomedical data are well curated, governed, documented, and shared in ways that meet FAIR and GA4GH standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Researchers actively use, contribute to, and help improve Sage’s data resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data sharing is responsible, ethical, and compliant, with appropriate access and minimal unnecessary friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;External scientists have well-coordinated and well-supported research experiences with Sage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your team has clear expectations, effective practices, and the support needed to deliver high-quality data stewardship and community programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data quality, metadata, and harmonization practices support cross-study and cross-consortium reuse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You identify opportunities for new projects, collaborations, and funding, including contributing to or leading competitive grant proposals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a trusted scientific and data stewardship partner to internal leadership and the external research community.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sage is well represented in large-scale Data Coordination Center (DCC) and consortium initiatives, including engagement with program officers, leading scientists, and other stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You balance strategic leadership, team development, and hands-on scientific contribution based on program needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Note:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please do not upload your resume as your cover letter (required)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Biomedical Data Science &amp;amp; Stewardship:&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applied Data Science:&lt;/strong&gt; Apply statistical, bioinformatic, and computational biology methods—including exploratory analysis, benchmarking, and tooling—to Sage’s large-scale, multi-omic data to improve usability, discoverability, and scientific value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Management &amp;amp; Curation:&lt;/strong&gt; Oversee the curation, organization, annotation, and lifecycle management of biomedical datasets in alignment with FAIR principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Governance:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Sage’s Privacy and Compliance Office to inform data governance frameworks and access-control models and ensure responsible, ethical, and compliant data sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Standards &amp;amp; Interoperability:&lt;/strong&gt; Champion FAIR principles and relevant GA4GH standards, including data-use ontologies, federated data access, and genomic data-sharing frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Quality &amp;amp; Harmonization:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead harmonization of complex, multi-source biomedical datasets to enable cross-study and cross-consortium analysis and reuse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk &amp;amp; Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt; Identify and manage data governance, privacy, and compliance risks across the data portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Community &amp;amp; Team Capability:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scientific Community Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Build and sustain a community of internal and external researchers through engagement programs, community meetings, documentation, and direct outreach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;External Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaborate with and coordinate the research of external scientists and consortium partners using Sage’s data, serving as a scientific liaison.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Hire, manage, and develop a multidisciplinary team of biomedical data managers, community engagement staff, and program managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Talent Development &amp;amp; Mentorship:&lt;/strong&gt; Mentor team members across data stewardship, computational biology, program management, and community engagement, supporting growth toward greater independence and technical leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI &amp;amp; Data Operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure effective tools, systems, and practices for data operations, including responsible use of AI-assisted and agentic workflows for curation, validation, and community support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Funding &amp;amp; Sustainability:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead grant proposals and funding strategies that support data infrastructure, program management, governance, and community programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish clear growth paths and continuously improve how Sage manages, governs, and builds community around its data in partnership with People Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Master’s or PhD&lt;/strong&gt; in a relevant scientific, data, or informatics discipline (e.g., biology, bioinformatics, data science, library/information science, or a related field), or equivalent depth of experience in lieu of an advanced degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced technical and domain expertise in data stewardship, applied analysis, and community-building, rather than an independent publication-focused research program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8+ years &lt;/strong&gt;of progressive experience in scientific research, biomedical data management, data governance, research data curation, or a closely related field, including leadership of complex, multi-stakeholder data or collaborative science initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in multi-institutional collaborations and consortia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3+ years&lt;/strong&gt; of experience directly managing, mentoring, and/or developing data managers, computational biologists, bioinformaticians, or community engagement professionals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of securing research funding as a principal investigator, co-investigator, or named key personnel, including at least one competitive NIH or comparable award.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience across the proposal lifecycle, including opportunity identification, partner collaboration, budget and effort planning, and post-award reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience applying open science and FAIR data principles and supporting responsible data sharing for human subjects data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GA4GH standards or comparable genomic/clinical data-sharing frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or activating a research community around a shared data resource or platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating with and coordinating external scientists or consortium partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing funder relationships and communicating scientific and data value to program officers and sponsors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate strategically while remaining close enough to data operations and community activity to identify and address emerging issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence decisions and create alignment across teams and leaders without relying solely on formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment and ability to navigate ambiguity, competing priorities, and evolving organizational needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with biomedical data standards and common data models, such as OMOP, FHIR, GA4GH Phenopackets, or Data Use Ontology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with data-sharing platforms and portals such as Synapse, dbGaP, or EGA and controlled-access data governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with NIH Genomic Data Sharing Policy, Data Management and Sharing Policy, or comparable funder requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience analyzing imaging and spatial biology data, including spatial transcriptomics, multiplexed tissue imaging, or digital pathology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI-assisted or agentic workflows for data curation, validation, or community support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with NIH-funded or comparable large-scale research consortia and public-private partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public-facing community engagement experience through conferences, working groups, newsletters, training programs, or similar activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing scientific, biomedical data management, or community-engagement career frameworks, competency models, or mentoring programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Functions and Physical Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The following cognitive and physical activities outline the essential functions required for successful job performance. Reasonable accommodations may be provided to enable individuals with disabilities to fulfill these functions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended periods of sitting at a desk and using a computer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Repeated wrist, hand, and finger movements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Requires clear vision for tasks like data analysis, transcribing, computer use, and reading.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasionally lifting or moving objects weighing up to 10 pounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cognitive Demands&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to work effectively under deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and analytical skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to detail and accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to adapt to changing environments, priorities and multitask.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Functions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel two times per year for on-site events in Seattle, WA.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective verbal and written communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works well in a team and maintains professionalism.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follows company policies, procedures, and relevant laws and regulations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Note: This list is not exhaustive and may be subject to modification as job duties evolve.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Total Rewards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sage Bionetworks implements equitable workplace strategies to ensure fair pay. Actual compensation is determined by market data, specific experience, and internal parity.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Job Level: &lt;strong&gt;Associate Director&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual Salary Range: &lt;strong&gt;$140,000 - $180,000&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Note: New hires typically receive an offer between the minimum and the midpoint of the range to allow for future growth within the role. Higher offers may be considered for exceptional experience or specific market conditions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comprehensive Benefits: We offer a package competitive with both commercial biotech and nonprofit sectors:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health &amp;amp; Wellness: Comprehensive medical, dental, vision, life, AD&amp;amp;D, and long-term disability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Future Security: Robust retirement plan and flexible spending accounts (FSA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work-Life Harmony: Paid time off and flexible work arrangements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://sagebionetworks.org/careers&quot;&gt;Learn more at: Benefits – Sage Bionetworks&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity &amp;amp; Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sage Bionetworks is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We prohibit discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Accommodation Request: If you require a reasonable accommodation during the application or interview process, please contact HR during the scheduling process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Modern Hiring &amp;amp; Responsible AI&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value your talent and your time. To ensure a fair and inclusive experience, we operate with the following principles:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible AI in Recruiting: To help us find the best talent, we may utilize AI tools within our recruiting platforms. We use these technologies responsibly to avoid the pitfalls of bias and discrimination. We believe technology should enhance human judgment, not replace it, and we regularly audit our processes to ensure every candidate is evaluated fairly based on their unique skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work from (Almost) Anywhere: We are a distributed workforce and support remote or hybrid arrangements within the United States.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Virtual-First Interviews: All interviews are conducted virtually to ensure accessibility and flexibility for all candidates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Sage Bionetworks: Science for the Common Good&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Sage Bionetworks, we believe the greatest barriers to medical progress aren&#39;t just biological—they are structural. Since 2009, our Seattle-founded nonprofit has been on a mission to tear down the &quot;silos&quot; of traditional science. We don’t just conduct research; we redefine how it’s done through open science, radical collaboration, and ethical data sharing.&lt;br&gt;When you join Sage, you aren&#39;t just taking a job; you’re joining a bold collective of scientists, engineers, governance experts, and visionaries. We empower patients to be partners, not just data points, and we provide the platforms that allow the global scientific community to accelerate life-saving discoveries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Sage Way: Our Core Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don’t just talk about change; we live it through these five pillars:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Science Driven: We use data and evidence to ensure our work creates a measurable, positive impact on human health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accountable: We deliver on our promises through a foundation of trust and radical transparency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth Oriented: We stay curious, seek out the hardest challenges, and constantly aspire to improve ourselves and our field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathetic + Inclusive: We embrace our differences and build environments where every voice is empowered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Radically Collaborative: We believe the best solutions come from teamwork and building diverse, global communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
